# <PROJECT NAME> — CLAUDE.md

This project uses Docket, attached at `<DOCKET_PATH>` (e.g.
`./docket` via symlink or submodule). This file is the entry point: it
establishes the Rules, the workflow, and this project's specific Project
Audit.

## Rules (non-negotiable)

See `<DOCKET_PATH>/core/RULES.md` for the full, current version — treat
it as authoritative and do not summarize around it. In short: every action
falls into CONFIRM (ask first), BLOCK (never do it), or unrestricted.
Destructive git operations, deletions, dependency changes, migrations,
anything touching secrets or production, are gated — read the source file,
don't rely on this summary for the actual rules.

## Workflow

See `<DOCKET_PATH>/core/WORKFLOW.md` for the full workflow. In short:
Ticket (planned and approved before code is written) → Implement → Self-review
→ Review (independent read-only check) → Done. No code is written before a
Ticket is approved.

## Roles

This project uses three Claude Code agents, defined in `.claude/agents/`,
sourced from `<DOCKET_PATH>/core/roles/`:

- **planner** — produces Tickets, no write access to code.
- **implementer** — scoped to the approved Ticket.
- **reviewer** — read-only tools, checks work against the Ticket before
  it's called done.

**At Review, spawn the `reviewer` subagent via the Agent tool — do not
review the work in the same conversation that just implemented it.** Give
it only the Ticket's file path and the diff against its baseline commit;
it should not inherit the Implement/Self-review conversation or reasoning.
This is the actual mechanism behind "independent check" in `WORKFLOW.md` —
a same-context role switch is not a substitute for it.

Tickets are created under `<TICKETS_PATH>` (e.g. `./tickets/`) using
`<DOCKET_PATH>/core/templates/ticket.template.md`.

